                <pb facs="0568" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg452"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.51/230: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cottrell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-01-03T10:00:00-04:32"><hi rendition="#italic">January 3,
                                1924—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1. Your number 27, December 28, 6 p.m. Congress has passed law as to Potosi-Sucre
                    Railroad and the President has signed it. I had previously protested as
                    requested.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cottrell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
